A||||5||JamesWM83||Sound like a starter?||||5||
Z||000000||JamesWM83||08-14-2001||01:30 AM||||Ok...my new 86 GT doesn't start unless it's started by popping the clutch while rolling. All the engine does is make a clicking noise everytime you turn the key. Sound like a bad starter? Solenoid? I really need to get this problem fixed... it's gonna be my daily driver and would look to have it runnin good and have reliable starting. After it starts... awesome. Love it. Thanks for any input. Lates||||reg||5
Z||000001||Pontiaddict||08-14-2001||03:45 AM||||Pull the starter and take it to a parts store. Most stores can usually bench test them.<p>[This message has been edited by Pontiaddict (edited 08-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Songman||08-14-2001||09:48 AM||||Sounds like it to me...<P>I just bought a lifetime warranty starter with solenoid for $49 at Advance. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||V8Dreamer||08-14-2001||04:20 PM||||Be sure to check battery and alternator also.....starter will make a clicking noise when battery is close to dead.  If this is the case, hopefully replacing the battery is your fix.<P>good luck,<BR>Ryan||||reg||1
Z||000004||Leadfoot||08-14-2001||04:46 PM||||Before you do anything, try this.  Get a jumper cable and hook one side to the engine and the other to the neg. side of the battery.  Then try starting it.  I had a similiar problem with my car.  It would only start when pushed.  After buying a battery and starter I found out it was a bad ground.||||reg||1
